  "id": "COMPOUND:42363 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Tubotaiwine is linked to Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through a series of molecular interactions involving a shared target compound, (1R,2R,4S,7Z,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-13-one. This compound acts as a target of Tubotaiwine and of several other entities, including MOVP-3 and VMRC-LCP, which in turn target the Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The evidence suggests that Tubotaiwine may inhibit the activity of this phosphatase through the direct or indirect action of the shared compound. The consistent presence of the same target compound across multiple pathways supports a mechanism where Tubotaiwine exerts its effects via this compound, potentially modulating the activity of the phosphatase. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for the compound in mediating the drug's interaction with the phosphatase, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
